---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Mouzi"
  description="The Mouzi privacy policy: the app collects no telemetry, while optional Google Analytics on mouzi.cc runs only after consent."
  canonical="/privacy"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <SectionHeading kicker="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lead="How Mouzi and mouzi.cc handle data." />

    <section class="prose mt-10">
      <h2>Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        The controller for optional website analytics is Krystian Welcel, the maintainer of Mouzi. Questions and GDPR
        requests can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.funding.contactEmail}`}>{site.funding.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The application</h2>
      <p>
        Mouzi processes files entirely on your device. The application does not collect, transmit or store any personal
        data on external servers. Specifically:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>No account or registration exists.</li>
        <li>No telemetry or analytics are sent.</li>
        <li>File names, paths and contents never leave your machine.</li>
        <li>Rules, settings and move history are stored locally and can be deleted by removing the configuration folder.</li>
        <li>
          The optional update check requests GitHub's public releases feed. This is a standard HTTPS request to
          GitHub and is subject to <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy policy</a>. You can disable it in settings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        mouzi.cc is a static site. If you allow optional analytics, it loads Google Analytics 4 using measurement ID
        <code>G-GMDTSE5DFS</code>. Google Analytics records page visits, session information, approximate location,
        and browser and device details. It may store a first-party client identifier in cookies whose names begin with
        <code>_ga</code>. It does not receive file names, paths, rules or other data from the Mouzi application.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Analytics does not load until you choose <strong>Allow analytics</strong>. Advertising storage, advertising
        user data and advertising personalization remain disabled. Your choice is saved locally in your browser under
        <code>mouzi-analytics-consent</code> for up to 180 days. You can change it below. See{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a> for information about
        Google's processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fonts and site assets are self-hosted. Download links point to GitHub Releases, where GitHub's policies apply.
        Sponsor links are ordinary links and sponsors cannot place tracking scripts on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Purpose and legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics is used to count visits, understand which documentation and download pages are useful, and find site
        navigation problems. When you click an official release download, the site records the Mouzi version, operating
        system, package type, file name and page containing the button. It does not record files from your computer or
        anything Mouzi organizes. The legal basis is your consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR. Refusing analytics does not
        limit the website, downloads or the Mouzi application. No analytics data is used for automated decisions or
        profiling by Mouzi.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies, retention and recipients</h2>
      <p>
        After consent, Google Analytics may set <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code> cookies to
        distinguish users and sessions. Google documents a default lifetime of up to two years, although browsers may
        shorten it. User-level and event-level information in a standard GA4 property may be retained for up to 14
        months. Aggregated reports may remain available for longer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Analytics data is processed by Google, including Google Ireland Limited for users in the EEA. Google may use
        infrastructure or subprocessors outside the EEA and describes its transfer safeguards, including applicable
        adequacy frameworks and Standard Contractual Clauses, in its{' '}
        <a href="https://business.safety.google/adsdatatransfers/" rel="noopener">international transfer information</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        The application does not send personal data to Mouzi. Local application data is under your control at
        <code>%APPDATA%\Mouzi</code> (Windows) or <code>~/.config/mouzi</code> (Linux).
      </p>
      <p>
        For website analytics data, you may request access, rectification, deletion or restriction where applicable.
        You may withdraw consent at any time without affecting processing that took place before withdrawal. You may
        also lodge a complaint with the{' '}
        <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl/en/681" rel="noopener">President of the Personal Data Protection Office (UODO)</a>
        in Poland or another competent supervisory authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button type="button" data-manage-analytics class="text-amber underline hover:no-underline">
          Change analytics preferences
        </button>
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.funding.contactEmail}`}>{site.funding.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Last updated: 9 August 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
